# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# Two ways to point at a database. DATABASE_URL wins if it is set.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A - hosted Supabase  (what to fill in for the real project)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string -> URI
#
# Pick the SESSION pooler (port 5432) or the direct connection. Do NOT use the
# transaction pooler on port 6543: it cannot run the DDL, prepared statements or
# advisory locks that migrations need, and it will fail halfway through 0006.
#
# Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password you set when the project was
# created. That is NOT the anon key and NOT your Supabase account password.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abcdefghijklm:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B - the local PostgreSQL install on this PC  (current default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PGHOST=localhost
PGPORT=5432
PGUSER=postgres
PGPASSWORD=your-local-postgres-password
PGDATABASE=cadence

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app's own connection  (used from P02 onward, not by the migration scripts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JS bundle and is therefore NOT secret. That is
# correct for these two: the anon key is designed to be public, and every table is
# protected by RLS. If a table is ever readable with only the anon key, the bug is a
# missing policy, not a leaked key.
#
# The service_role key must NEVER appear in this file, in the app, or in git. It
# bypasses RLS completely, which would defeat every guarantee P01 built.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://abcdefghijklm.supabase.co
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Applying the schema to a hosted project
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   node supabase/db.mjs migrate      applies 0001..0012. Forward only, drops nothing.
#   node supabase/gen-types.mjs       regenerates the TypeScript types from it.
#
# `reset` and `seed` refuse to run against a remote host on purpose: reset drops the
# database, and seed forges rows in auth.users. Both are local-only tools.
#
# The shim in supabase/local/ is NOT applied to a hosted project and must not be -
# Supabase already provides auth.uid(), the storage schema and the roles.
